  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Equitable Access to Sufficient and Safe Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Services for Vulnerable Conflict-Affected Populations in Kyiv Oblast</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The invasion of Ukraine on 24 February resulted in the displacement of nearly 6.3 million people as of 23 June 2022 (IOM Displacement Report Round 6). The overall scale and unpredictability of the situation requires immediate humanitarian assistance for the most vulnerable displaced and conflict-affected communities. This project aims to enhance equitable access to sufficient and safe water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) services for the most vulnerable conflict-affected populations in Kyiv oblast, Main activities include support for enhancing local and national water associations&apos; and companies&apos; response capacity and water supply systems.</narrative>
  </description>
